      "content": "GridScale Deploy automates container orchestration by managing your application lifecycles within Kubernetes clusters, streamlining the path from local development to production. Before running any commands, confirm that both Docker is installed to build images and kubectl is configured to communicate with your cluster's API server. To initialize your new project, execute `gs-deploy init`, which scans your source code and generates the necessary manifest files against the pattern defined in your template repository. Once initialized, use the `gs-deploy up --env prod` command to stage your changes, build the Docker image, and push it to the specified cluster environment. Your application will then begin running and listening on the default port, 8080, accessible via the internal service DNS or external load balancer depending on your cluster settings.",
