      "content": "that's better, but the automated completeness score is still coming back pretty low compared to our other docs. it's looking more like a paragraph than a full guide.\n\ncan we make this even more robust? maybe include a troubleshooting section, a brief explanation of why we use docker/kubectl, and some more detailed steps for the init process. just make sure it's a really \"meaty\" document. i know i said not to pad it earlier, but i'd rather have a slightly long, thorough guide that satisfies the completeness metric than a short one that looks \"incomplete\" in the system. thanks!",
